## Why This Is Asked

Assesses capability to design scalable, tenant-aware CAPA for a shared data platform, balancing fairness and speed while ensuring traceability.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and backpressure control
- Evidence collection and artifact management
- Lifecycle state machine design
- REST API design for CAPA with logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics and RCA structuring
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  onset: string;
  status: string;
  logs: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you store and query cross-tenant artifacts at scale?
- What tests would validate canary safety under burst traffic?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around operational risk in alert routing, including change control, cross-tenant impact, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model (evidence, lineage, owners)
- Lifecycle with detect/contain/remediate/verify and SLAs
- Canary-based rollback and change control
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, MTTR

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express-like minimal CAPA create endpoint (illustrative)
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const capa = req.body;
  // persist CAPA with evidence, lineage, owners
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', ...capa });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollback plan for alert-rule changes?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate containment and prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests CAPA fundamentals under real-world data issues: region awareness, basic data modeling, and a simple remediation flow.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model, lifecycle, REST API, regional metrics, RCA, canary.
- Trade-offs: latency of detection vs noise, data retention for evidence.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express REST endpoints
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let store = [];
app.post('/caps', (req, res)=>{ const cap={id:Date.now().toString(), ...req.body, status:'detected', created_at:new Date().toISOString()}; store.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
app.put('/caps/:id', (req,res)=>{ const idx=store.findIndex(c=>c.id===req.params.id); if(idx>=0){store[idx]={...store[idx], ...req.body}; res.json(store[idx]);} else res.status(404).end();});
app.listen(3000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate and test the canary plan before broader rollout?
- What telemetry would you capture to ensure no regression after remediation?

